  "summary": "Validating Matrix Content URIs may panic",
  "details": "Using `mxc_uri::validate` may panic if the server name part of the URI is larger\nthan 249 bytes. The affected versions assumed that the length of the first part\nof the URI (`mxc://{server_name}`) would fit into a `NonZeroU8`, but the length\nof the server name wasn't validated and the Matrix specification actually allows\nthe server name to have a maximum length of 261 bytes.",
